			"date": "2024-07-03T13:32:31.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> oh yeah, they seem to have a rule to forbid a++ but not one to forbid +a (as far as I can see) when unary plus is exclusively used for terrible cursed type munging and should be binned off along with the comma operator</p><p>that wouldn't help with -= but i mean it's something</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
