			"date": "2024-07-03T13:32:41.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> From an AST perspective, it's code that humans might write; `x = +string_or_number` will coerce `string_or_number` to a number. The d3 source code uses this idiom a lot, for example.</p><p>(Obviously you might still want an eslint rule that disallows this idiom, but typescript definitely shouldn't/can't flag it imo)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
